            <div xml:id="d749">

                <pb facs="0863" n="853" sameAs="frus:frus1948v08/pg853"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1115/10–1848: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Stuart</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-10-19T18:00:00-05:00">October 19, 1948—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1469. Dept opinion proposed text warning (your 1926, Oct. 18) unnecessarily
                    explicit and may have unduly damaging effect Nationalist position north China.
                    Fol[lowing] substitute phraseology recommended: <pb facs="0864" n="854"
                        xml:id="pg854"/>
                    <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Military situation north China appears to indicate that hostilities may
                            spread to areas hitherto peaceful and that normal transportation
                            facilities may be completely disrupted. Accordingly American citizens
                            should consider desirability evacuation at this time while normal
                            transportation facilities are still available.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lovett</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
